From: Grant McNaught <1371263+gmcnaught@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 01:05:09 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 34/40] chore: remove resident_static_before_animated (dead
 after ARGB4444 plane bake)

The ARGB4444/PALPHA plane bake (Task 5/6, host-side only -- not part of this
patch series) gives every baked plane real per-pixel alpha, so its one-shot
full-frame COPY is safe to fire wherever the per-bucket static-replay path
already fires (after animated ops, patch 0031) on every layer -- including
the base layer. That made Renderer::resident_static_before_animated() (added
by patch 0032, needed by the old base-layer-only opaque-COPY design)
permanently return false from every override, and the _static_first branch
in Entities::draw() dead. Delete the base virtual and restore the
unconditional animated-then-static order patch 0031 established.
---
 src/entities/Entities.cpp | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/entities/Entities.cpp b/src/entities/Entities.cpp
index 18d5d3c..a3813b4 100644
--- a/src/entities/Entities.cpp
+++ b/src/entities/Entities.cpp
@@ -1536,6 +1536,15 @@ void Entities::draw() {
       // of behind it. Static-after-animated restores the vanilla result: static content
       // occludes the background wherever it's placed, and the background only shows
       // through the gaps -- with zero cost, since this is just a call-order swap.
+      //
+      // [Phase 3b/Task 7] Static always fires AFTER animated now, unconditionally, for
+      // every layer including any baked-plane renderer's one-shot full-frame COPY: the
+      // ARGB4444/PALPHA bake (Task 5/6) gives every plane real per-pixel alpha, so its
+      // COPY leaves gaps untouched and is safe to fire here regardless of what else
+      // drew first this frame. The prior "fire the plane's opaque COPY before anything
+      // else on its layer" special case (Renderer::resident_static_before_animated,
+      // needed by the old base-layer-only opaque-COPY design) is gone -- removed along
+      // with the virtual itself (see Renderer.h).
       const int _nops = R.resident_layer_op_count(layer);
       for (int _oi = 0; _oi < _nops; ++_oi) R.resident_emit_layer_op(layer, _oi);
       if (_tilestatic) {
